course: dictionary
lesson: 15664
title: Tho: a short way of writing though
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tho is a short, casual way of writing though. You will see it in texts, chats and comics, where a character talks like a friend. It is informal, so it is fine to read it, but do not use it in school writing.
explain: «The cake looked nice, tho it was a bit burnt.» Tho adds a small but: the cake looked nice, but it was burnt. Try swapping in but or though. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: Tho can also mean even if it is true that. «I'll go to the park, tho I'm a bit tired.» Here tho means I'll go even though I'm tired. Read the whole sentence to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Tho often comes at the end of a sentence, as in «Nice tho.» That means it was nice, but there is a small catch. In your own writing, always use though or although instead.
fact: Tho is an informal, short spelling of though.
fact: Tho usually means but or however.
fact: Tho can also mean even if it is true that, like although.
fact: Tho often sits at the end of a sentence, as in «Nice tho» or «Tho I guess».
fact: In school writing, use though or although, not tho.
exercise: «The party was fun tho, I was tired.» What does tho mean here? | Another party | A short walk | Very loudly | * But, meaning however
exercise: Which is the correct school-writing spelling of tho? | Thorough | Thou | * Though | Thaw
exercise: Ella writes «I'll come tho I'm busy.» What does tho mean? | Thoroughly | Very busy and tired | * Even if it is true that, so: even though I'm busy | A kind of coming
test: «The sun came out, tho it was still cold.» What should you write instead of tho in school writing? | Thaw | * Though | Thou | Tow
test: «Nice tho.» What does the tho add to the sentence? | Loudness | * A small but: it was nice, however | A question about the niceness | Speed
exam: Mia writes «I'll go tho I'm sick.» What should she write in school? | * I'll go although I'm sick | I'll go tho I'm sick | I'll go thaw I'm sick | I'll go thou I'm sick
